> sure; when Doug McLain did the repairs to wordclock and spdif for the ice1712 
> driver so he could run multiple Delta 1010's, he also got the sync "led" on 
> the hardware page to function in the envy24control panel. On the C-Port 
> however this "led"  doesn't even appear, so there is no way of knowing when 
> you have sync over multiple cards. Also, envy24control won't sync the cards 
> properly using spdif ( c-port doesn't have wordclock)... i have to use 
> alsamixer to sync them reliably.

The word clock sync controls are implemented only for M-audio delta
boards.  No other boards, e.g. TerraTec or Hoontech, have this
feature.  That is, no equivalent hardware functionality is given on
these boards (at least, no information how to implement).


